\newlabel{fig:app-exp24-alpha-canon}{{10}{19}{\textbf {Identity variance with alpha-canonicalized variants (Fig-9-style bars).} Blue: original identity variance; orange/green: alpha-canonicalized proxies (drop/clip). Across judges, canonicalization substantially reduces identity variance (mean reduction: \(53.2\%\) for drop, \(57.6\%\) for clip), indicating that alpha-renaming sensitivity is a dominant variance source}{figure.caption.51}{}}
